{
  "id": "goldbeter-mitotic-cascade-biology",
  "name": "Goldbeter cyclin-kinase-protease mitotic cascade",
  "description": "Cyclin concentration drives two conserved active/inactive enzyme fractions. Fractions are not clipped. Uses adaptive Radau because small enzyme saturation produces sharp transitions. Coefficients and all initial states0.01 independently transcribed from the primary-model exposure: https://models.physiomeproject.org/e/4c/goldbeter_annotated_1991.cellml . K1=K2=K3=K4=.005 share one equivalent parameter. Horizon100min, outputdt.25 and solver tolerances are our verification choices; no CellML code or article prose copied. Signed net-rate flows encode equations, not material transfer claims. No clamps or hidden state resets.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.88.20.9107",
  "reference": "Goldbeter (1991), A minimal cascade model for the mitotic oscillator involving cyclin and cdc2 kinase. Parameter/state cross-check: Physiome Goldbeter1991 exposure4c, changeset930898d5d5f4.",
